title: SIP Hijack - CryptSIPDllVerifyIndirectData Registry Modification
id: a7c3e9f1-2b4d-4e8a-9c1f-3d5e7f8a0b2c
status: experimental
description: |
    Detects any write to the PE SIP GUID registry key for CryptSIPDllVerifyIndirectData.
    An attacker registering a rogue DLL export as the PE SIP verify handler causes
    WinVerifyTrust to return S_OK for any PE regardless of signature validity.
    Covers both the 8E78 (CryptSIPDllGetSignedDataMsg) and 14B6 (CryptSIPDllVerifyIndirectData)
    variant GUIDs under {C689AAB8}.
references:
    - lab/poc/sip-hijack/loader.ps1
    - https://specterops.io/wp-content/uploads/sites/3/2022/06/SpecterOps_Subverting_Trust_in_Windows.pdf
author: Research
date: 2026-06-04
modified: 2026-06-04
tags:
    - attack.defense_evasion
    - attack.t1553.002
logsource:
    product: windows
    category: registry_set
detection:
    selection_key:
        EventID: 13
        TargetObject|contains:
            - 'CryptSIPDllVerifyIndirectData'
    selection_guid:
        TargetObject|contains:
            - 'C689AAB8-14B6-11d2-BD56-0000F803049C'
            - 'C689AAB8-8E78-11d2-BD56-0000F803049C'
    condition: selection_key and selection_guid
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate SIP provider registration by security software (rare; legitimate tools
      register at install time, not at runtime from PowerShell or sc.exe)
    - Developer workflows using mattifestation/PoCSubjectInterfacePackage for testing
level: high
fields:
    - TargetObject
    - Details
    - Image
    - User
